[2026-08-18 15:11:07] [agentic_rollout_pipeline.py (134)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 1310266] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Tic-Tac-Toe.user\nChoose exactly one legal move that maximizes your final game outcome:\nwin is better than draw, and draw is better than loss.\n\nAnalyze the strategy as concisely as possible and choose exactly one legal action.\nDo not enumerate every legal move or the complete game tree.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>one brief reason</reason>\n<answer><SYMBOL(row,column)></answer>\n\nDo not output anything else.Information of Turn-1:\n\nThis is the other player's turn. The game state, legal actions, as well as the chosen action of the other player for this turn are provided below.\n\nGAME STATE:\n___\n___\n___\n\nLEGAL ACTIONS:\nX(0,0), X(0,1), X(0,2), X(1,0), X(1,1), X(1,2), X(2,0), X(2,1), X(2,2).\n\nCHOSEN ACTION:\nX(1,1)\n\n\nYou are player O.\n\nBoard:\n  0 1 2\n0 . . .\n1 . X .\n2 . . .\n\nLegal moves:\nO(0,0), O(0,1), O(0,2), O(1,0), O(1,2), O(2,0), O(2,1), O(2,2)assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Player X is already in (1,1), so center is occupied. To maximize win chance, O should block X's potential to complete a row, column, or diagonal. The center is taken, so O should aim to create a winning opportunity or block X's winning lines. The only immediate threat is X completing a diagonal or row. However, O(0,0) threatens a diagonal with O(0,0), O(1,1), O(2,2), which is currently blocked at (1,1). Instead, O(2,0) attacks the bottom-left and supports potential future lines. But best move: O(0,0) controls the top-left corner, enabling future diagonal or row development. However, (0,0) is not directly winning. Best strategic move is O(2,2) to mirror X's position and threaten a diagonal. But (1,1) is X. So O(0,2) or O(2,0) could complete a line. Actually, X has no immediate win path. O should take center — but center taken. So O(0,0) opens a path to win in future. However, O(2,0) is symmetric. Most critical: O(0,2) or O(2,0) — both ope